{"concerns":[{"severity":"P2","kind":"failure_mode","message":"Several existing specs check the pages this lane rewrites, but the lane only runs ux-review.spec.ts. guardrails.spec.ts:111-136 checks the challenge page: the `challenge-severity` groups, the 'pauses the run unless accepted' heading, `challenge-attempts` reading '2 attempts; this is attempt 2', and the P2 `challenge-consequence` exact text via toHaveText. ux-node.spec.ts:103-107 and projects.spec.ts:308-310 require `result-none` and `events-none` on an integrate step that has not started. projects.spec.ts:324-325 and review.spec.ts:150 require `awaiting-notice` to keep 'Viewing does not approve it' and the approval_requested message. The task names only reviewers.spec.ts:86 and review.spec.ts as must-stay-green.","consequence":"A headline that replaces `challenge-attempts` or the severity headings, P2 consequences rendered only once expanded, or a ControllerSections that drops `renderResult`/`result-none` would pass the lane's own run. It would then fail verify_panels and the combined candidate, costing a repair attempt against the cap of 3. projects.spec.ts belongs to the lists lane, so neither lane would notice before the verifier."},{"severity":"P2","kind":"assumption","message":"The integrate panel must name the fast-forwarded branch and commit, but the served data does not hold them directly. Only a real controller writes the commit in the event message ('Fast-forwarded to <sha>; no push performed', pipeline.py:623). Seeded runs say 'Fast-forwarded the feature branch', and `integrated_commit` is not in the contract (server/projects.ts:328 only uses it for status). The served sources are `inputs.source_branch` (nullable) and the review result's `candidate_commit`, which is what integrate fast-forwards to. On the approval and integrate pages the review resource must be keyed on the review node's `result_uri` or attempt, not on the node being viewed.","consequence":"If the commit is parsed from the event message, older exports and existing seeds show no commit. If the review is fetched for `node` (approval or integrate) instead of the review node, there is no bundle hash or commit on those pages."},{"severity":"P2","kind":"assumption","message":"The controller never writes an event for the approval node: pipeline.py has no `self.event("approval", …)`, and an awaiting approval node gets its status from LangGraph interrupts (server/projects.ts:1308). So 'no approval event recorded' is always true. 'Approved automatically by the finish policy (…)' is only right when `inputs.mode` is automatic; a manual run is approved by the operator's `approve`. PRD 4.9's 'Awaiting your approval since …, taken from the node's last status event' has no such event in real runs.","consequence":"If the wording ignores `inputs.mode`, manual runs are mislabelled as policy approvals. If the fixture seeds an approval status event so that 'since' renders, the test passes on data real runs never produce, and production shows nothing or the wrong time."},{"severity":"P2","kind":"failure_mode","message":"The approve command with the bundle hash in `node-next` comes from RunView's `deriveNow`. It reads the review only through the review node's `result_uri` (RunView.tsx:80) and has no `paths.review` fallback; otherwise it writes the literal '<bundle sha256>' (triage.ts:1090). The fixture's manual awaiting-approval run needs a review node `result_uri` in both phases. The command should also be shown once (in `node-next`), not repeated in `awaiting-notice`.","consequence":"If the fixture has no review `result_uri`, controller-panels fails its hash assertion in one phase, or the worker duplicates the command with its own hash to get the test green."},{"severity":"P2","kind":"failure_mode","message":"`expectNoExecutionControls` rejects any button whose text, including its descendants, matches /approve|retry|launch|start|resume|delete|cancel|integrate|edit|save/i. The new content contains those words: the paused challenge's P1 text, 'no worker launched', 'edit the feature files', finding messages, and the integrate line. A toggle for expanding a P2 concern or a card's 'More' that wraps this text in a <button> trips the guard.","consequence":"guardrails, ux-review or review specs fail on a <button> that holds a concern or finding message. Using <details>/<summary> for P2 concerns and card expansion avoids this, and it also keeps the concern text in the DOM, where `toHaveText` reads it."},{"severity":"P2","kind":"assumption","message":"The handoff's 'latest launch start' is ambiguous. The receipt has both `launch_requested_at` and a nullable `native_started_at`, and inputs keep only each lane's latest receipt. PRD 4.9 and 12.1 give the same 28m21s for the handoff wait and the worker span from receipts.","consequence":"If panels.ts computes the wait separately from `buildTimeline`'s worker span, the handoff says one duration and the launch node another for the same interval. That contradicts the PRD example and confuses the operator."}],"simpler_alternative":"Make every S4c change additive to the markup that exists today. Keep `ChallengePanel`'s test ids, severity groups and wording. Put the one-line headline above it (outcome, attempt, notes, `decided_at`, span from the timeline). Turn each P2 `<li>` into a `<details>` whose summary is the one-line message and whose body keeps `challenge-consequence`. Keep `renderResult` (with `result-none`) and History in ControllerSections, and add one computed line per controller node from pure panels.ts helpers:
- handoff wait: the timeline's worker span end to the freeze event;
- approval: ≈ instant plus policy or operator wording by `inputs.mode`;
- integrate: `source_branch` plus the review's `candidate_commit`.
For the review, render the blocking cards as a sibling before `review-findings` and restyle the one table with a ≤760 px media query. Nothing that other specs check is removed, so the lane's narrow test run is enough evidence.","cheap_experiment":"In a scratch worktree, make three throwaway edits:
1. Wrap each P2 challenge concern in `<details>`.
2. Replace ControllerSections' body with a static line.
3. Replace `challenge-attempts` with a headline.

Then run `WORKFLOW_VERIFICATION_PHASE=candidate npx --no-install playwright test --config=tests/project-workflows/playwright.config.ts guardrails.spec.ts ux-node.spec.ts projects.spec.ts review.spec.ts reviewers.spec.ts`. It takes minutes. It shows exactly which existing assertions constrain the panels' markup. That decides whether the redesign can replace ChallengePanel and ControllerSections or has to stay additive, and whether the panels lane should add those spec files to its targeted run."}

